From: gugu-acp <gugu-acp@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 16:35:43 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] gugu: accept the personal provider table as content
 (ZCODE_PERSONAL_PROVIDER_CONFIG_CONTENT)

A host that hands one bridge process its own provider table can pass the
whole table in ZCODE_PERSONAL_PROVIDER_CONFIG_CONTENT. At startup (main and
runHeadless) the bridge writes it into a private 0600 file in a fresh 0700
temp directory, points ZCODE_PERSONAL_PROVIDER_CONFIG_FILE at it (0005), drops
the content variable from its own environment so children never inherit it,
and removes the directory on process exit. Content that is not JSON throws:
a host that meant to pin the provider must not fall back to the user's own
table. A SIGKILLed bridge leaves the file behind (no exit hook runs).

Why: Gugu delivers platform-model configuration to an ACP adapter process as
one environment variable carrying the whole document (the same carrier its
other harnesses use); the ZCode backend only reads a file.

Measured: an isolated HOME with no provider table, only the content variable
-> the model menu lists only the session's provider, a turn completes, and
no zcode-acp-provider-* directory is left after exit.

Upstream: not filed - owner 10-17: kept and maintained here only (see
bridges/zcode-acp/PATCHES.md for the upstream code it touches).

Drop when: never while Gugu hands the table as content; re-check on upgrade
that both entry points (main, runHeadless) still run it before the server
exists.
